(1249, 1, '2024-04-30 15:59:59', '2024-04-30 20:59:59', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/heading {\"clientId\":\"ec22a58a\",\"text\":\"Gardens\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"blockart-heading blockart-heading-ec22a58a\">Gardens</h2>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/section {\"clientId\":\"817853d4\",\"columns\":2} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-section blockart-section-817853d4\"><div class=\"blockart-container\"><div class=\"blockart-section-inner\"><!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"61415c5d\",\"colWidth\":{\"desktop\":66,\"tablet\":100,\"mobile\":100}} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-61415c5d\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Japanese gardens are exquisite landscapes that transcend mere horticulture, embodying a profound connection between nature, spirituality, and aesthetic harmony. Rooted in centuries-old traditions, these meticulously designed spaces are a reflection of the Japanese philosophy of finding beauty in simplicity and<br>balance. Elements such as carefully raked gravel, serene ponds, meticulously pruned trees, and strategically placed rocks create a harmonious composition that invites contemplation and a sense of tranquility.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"3723d98a\",\"colWidth\":{\"desktop\":34,\"tablet\":100,\"mobile\":100}} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-3723d98a\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:blockart/image {\"clientId\":\"ffe40e95\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/pexels-bagus41-1440476-1-scaled.jpg\",\"id\":1248,\"alt\":\"\"}} -->\n<figure class=\"blockart-image blockart-image-ffe40e95\"><img class=\"wp-image-1248 hover-effect-static filter-none mask mask-none\" src=\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/pexels-bagus41-144047