":{\"right\":10,\"unit\":\"px\",\"lock\":false,\"left\":10},\"dimension\":1}} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-section blockart-section-73b9fc42\"><div class=\"blockart-container\"><div class=\"blockart-section-inner\"><!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"82718716\",\"blockMargin\":{\"desktop\":{\"lock\":true,\"unit\":\"px\"},\"tablet\":{\"bottom\":50,\"unit\":\"px\",\"lock\":false},\"mobile\":{\"bottom\":50,\"unit\":\"px\",\"lock\":false},\"dimension\":1},\"blockPadding\":{\"desktop\":{\"lock\":true,\"unit\":\"px\"},\"dimension\":1}} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-82718716\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Japanese gardens are exquisite landscapes that transcend mere horticulture, embodying a profound connection between nature, spirituality, and aesthetic harmony. Rooted in centuries-old traditions, these meticulously designed spaces are a reflection of the Japanese philosophy of finding beauty in simplicity and balance. Elements such as carefully raked gravel, serene ponds, meticulously pruned trees, and strategically placed rocks create a harmonious composition that invites contemplation and a sense of tranquility.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/button {\"clientId\":\"6f8dece4\",\"justification\":{\"desktop\":\"left\",\"tablet\":\"left\"},\"orientation\":{\"desktop\":\"horizontal\"}} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-buttons blockart-buttons-6f8dece4 is-wrap is-horizontal justify-left justify-left-md\"><!-- wp:blockart/button-inner {\"clientId\":\"c78b4dbf\",\"text\":\"Read More\",\"size\":\"custom\",\"padding\":{\"dimension\":1,\"desktop\":{\"lock\":false,\"top\":16,\"right\":36,\"bottom\":16,\"left\":36,\"unit\":\"px\"}},\"typography\":{\"typography\":1,\"weight\":500,\"size\":{\"desktop\":{\"value\":16,\"unit\":\"px\"},\"mobile\":{\"value\":16,\"unit\":\"px\"}},\"family\":\"Poppins\"},\"color1\":\"#000000\",\"color2\":\"#ffffff\",\"hoverColor1\":\"#ffffff\",\"hoverColor2\":\"#000000\",\"background1\":{\"