683x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Woman Eating Sushi in a Restaurant\" height=\"1024\" width=\"683\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/image -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/spacing {\"clientId\":\"6901ae06\"} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-spacing blockart-spacing-6901ae06\"><div class=\"blockart-spacing-inner\"></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/spacing -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/heading {\"clientId\":\"0b9ba7aa\",\"text\":\"Saké—the Perfect Accompaniment\",\"alignment\":{\"desktop\":\"left\"},\"size\":\"small\",\"typography\":{\"typography\":1,\"weight\":\"600\",\"family\":\"Poppins\",\"size\":{\"desktop\":{\"value\":30,\"unit\":\"px\"}},\"lineHeight\":{\"desktop\":{\"value\":28,\"unit\":\"px\"}}}} -->\n<h2 class=\"blockart-heading blockart-heading-0b9ba7aa is-small\">Saké—the Perfect Accompaniment</h2>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Japanese rice wine, saké, makes the perfect accompaniment to your meal. Although saké can be drunk hot, connoisseurs prefer to drink it cold or on the rocks. Drinking saké cold allows you to appreciate the subtle differences in taste that come from the rice variety and water used in the fermentation process.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column --></div></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/section --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column --></div></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/section -->', 'Reservations', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '1315-revision-v1', '', '', '2024-05-05 00:40:51', '2024-05-05 05:40:51', '', 1315, 'https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/?p=1317', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
