";b:1;s:9:\"rest_base\";s:0:\"\";s:14:\"rest_namespace\";s:5:\"wp/v2\";s:21:\"rest_controller_class\";s:24:\"WP_REST_Posts_Controller\";s:13:\"menu_position\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"menu_icon\";s:0:\"\";s:19:\"rename_capabilities\";b:0;s:24:\"singular_capability_name\";s:4:\"post\";s:22:\"plural_capability_name\";s:5:\"posts\";s:8:\"supports\";a:3:{i:0;s:5:\"title\";i:1;s:6:\"editor\";i:2;s:9:\"thumbnail\";}s:10:\"taxonomies\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"has_archive\";b:0;s:16:\"has_archive_slug\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"rewrite\";a:4:{s:17:\"permalink_rewrite\";s:13:\"post_type_key\";s:10:\"with_front\";s:1:\"1\";s:5:\"feeds\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"pages\";s:1:\"1\";}s:9:\"query_var\";s:13:\"post_type_key\";s:14:\"query_var_name\";s:0:\"\";s:10:\"can_export\";b:1;s:16:\"delete_with_user\";b:0;s:20:\"register_meta_box_cb\";s:0:\"\";s:16:\"enter_title_here\";s:0:\"\";}', 'Blogs', 'blogs', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'post_type_6639206cda77e', '', '', '2024-05-06 13:25:00', '2024-05-06 18:25:00', '', 0, 'https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/?post_type=acf-post-type&#038;p=1400', 0, 'acf-post-type', '', 0),
(1401, 1, '2024-05-06 13:32:54', '2024-05-06 18:32:54', '<!-- wp:kadence/rowlayout {\"uniqueID\":\"1401_a732fc-7e\",\"columns\":1,\"collapseGutter\":\"skinny\",\"customRowGutter\":[10,\"\",\"\"],\"colLayout\":\"equal\",\"bgImg\":\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/free-stock-photo-of-early-sunrise-hiking-adventures-huauchinango-22492024-1024x683.jpg\",\"bgImgPosition\":\"43% 50%\",\"padding\":[\"5xl\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],\"kbVersion\":2} -->\n<!-- wp:kadence/column {\"borderWidth\":[\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],\"uniqueID\":\"1401_c0b65b-ad\",\"kbVersion\":2} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-column kadence-column1401_c0b65b-ad\"><div class=\"kt-inside-inner-col\"><!-- wp:ultimate-post/heading {\"blockId\":\"384620\",\"headingText\":\"Hiking\",\"headingStyle\":\"style7\",\"headingTag\":\"h1\",\"headingTypo\":{\"openTypography\":1,\"size\":{\"lg\":\"55\",\"unit\":\"px\"},\"height\":{\"lg\":\"\",\"unit\":\"px\"},\"decoration\":\"none\",\"transform\":\"\",\"family\":\"Poppins\",\"weight\":\"700i\",\"type\":\"sans-serif\"},\"headingColor\":\"#ffffff\",\"headingBorderBottomColor\":\"#ffffff\"} /--></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:kadence/column -->\n<!-- /wp:kadence/rowlayout -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {\"ref\":1421} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Hiking in Japan offers a diverse range of landscapes, from towering mountains to serene coastal trails, providing outdoor enthusiasts with a variety of options to explore the country\'s natural beauty. Here are some notable hiking destinations and considerations for hiking in Japan:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/section {\"clientId\":\"a7162eff\",\"columns\":2} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-section blockart-section-a7162eff\"><div class=\"blockart-container\"><div class=\"blockart-section-inner\"><!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"71223f70\"} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-71223f70\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Kumano Kodo: This ancient pilgrimage route on the Kii Peninsula takes hikers through lush forests, picturesque valleys, and historic shrines. The Nakahechi route is particularly popular, leading to the Kumano Hongu Taisha Grand Shrine.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/paragraph {\"clientId\":\"e2f1d306\",\"text\":\"Hakusan National Park: Mount Hakusan, located in central Japan, is known for its challenging yet rewarding hikes. The mountain is a sacred site and offers various trails, each providing stunning views of alpine landscapes and, during the summer, vibrant alpine flowers.\"} -->\n<p class=\"blockart-paragraph blockart-paragraph-e2f1d306\">Hakusan National Park: Mount Hakusan, located in central Japan, is known for its challenging yet rewarding hikes. The mountain is a sacred site and offers various trails, each providing stunning views of alpine landscapes and, during the summer, vibrant alpine flowers.</p>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"0ce01102\"} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-0ce01102\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/blooming-sakura-tree-against-residential-buildings-and-ridge-in-countryside-6136511-1024x683.jpg\",\"id\":1369,\"alt\":\"Blooming Sakura tree against residential buildings and ridge in countryside\",\"dimRatio\":0,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.36,\"y\":0.69},\"isDark\":false,\"style\":{\"color\":{}}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim-0 has-background-dim\"></span><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-1369\" alt=\"Blooming Sakura tree against residential buildings and ridge in countryside\" src=\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/blooming-sakura-tree-against-residential-buildings-and-ridge-in-countryside-6136511-1024x683.jpg\" style=\"object-position:36% 69%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"36% 69%\"/><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\",\"fontSize\":\"large\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-large-font-size\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column --></div></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/spacing {\"clientId\":\"0e8ea92c\",\"height\":{\"desktop\":{\"value\":15,\"unit\":\"px\"}}} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-spacing blockart-spacing-0e8ea92c\"><div class=\"blockart-spacing-inner\"></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/spacing -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Kamikochi: Nestled in the Northern Japan Alps, Kamikochi is a highland valley with scenic trails along the Azusa River. The landscapes include majestic peaks, serene lakes, and the iconic Hotaka Mountain Range.</span></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Hiking', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'hiking', '', '', '2024-05-07 13:38:49', '2024-05-07 18:38:49', '', 0, 'https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/?post_type=blog&#038;p=1401', 0, 'blog', '', 0),
(1402, 1, '2024-05-06 13:30:51', '2024-05-06 18:30:51', '<!-- wp:kadence/rowlayout {\"uniqueID\":\"1402_03b622-82\",\"columns\":1,\"collapseGutter\":\"skinny\",\"customRowGutter\":[10,\"\",\"\"],\"colLayout\":\"equal\",\"bgImg\":\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/a-woman-holding-a-teapot-8952398-683x1024.jpg\",\"bgImgPosition\":\"60% 44%\",\"padding\":[\"5xl\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],\"kbVersion\":2} -->\n<!-- wp:kadence/column {\"borderWidth\":[\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],\"uniqueID\":\"1402_6065b1-77\",\"kbVersion\":2} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-column kadence-column1402_6065b1-77\"><div class=\"kt-inside-inner-col\"><!-- wp:ultimate-post/heading {\"blockId\":\"0ace9c\",\"headingText\":\"Tea Ceremony\",\"headingStyle\":\"style7\",\"headingTag\":\"h1\",\"headingTypo\":{\"openTypography\":1,\"size\":{\"lg\":\"55\",\"unit\":\"px\"},\"height\":{\"lg\":\"\",\"unit\":\"px\"},\"decoration\":\"none\",\"transform\":\"\",\"family\":\"Poppins\",\"weight\":\"700i\",\"type\":\"sans-serif\"},\"headingColor\":\"#ffffff\",\"headingBorderBottomColor\":\"#ffffff\"} /--></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:kadence/column -->\n<!-- /wp:kadence/rowlayout -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {\"ref\":1421} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/section {\"clientId\":\"75920419\",\"columns\":2} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-section blockart-section-75920419\"><div class=\"blockart-container\"><div class=\"blockart-section-inner\"><!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"42115cae\"} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-42115cae\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Japanese tea ceremony, known as \"chanoyu\" or \"chado,\" is a traditional ritual influenced by Zen Buddhism in which powdered green tea, or matcha, is ceremonially prepared by a skilled practitioner and served to a small group of guests in a tranquil setting. The ceremony emphasizes harmony, respect, purity, and tranquility, encapsulating principles deeply rooted in Japanese culture.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The tea ceremony is often conducted in a purpose-built tea room or a tea house within a traditional garden. The setting is carefully chosen to create a serene atmosphere conducive to meditation and appreciation of the moment. The ceremony is not just about drinking tea; it is a cultural experience that involves aesthetics, etiquette, and a profound connection with nature.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"d7d99338\"} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-d7d99338\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":1362,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/a-geisha-in-red-kimono-preparing-a-tea-8748544-683x1024.jpg\" alt=\"A Geisha in Red Kimono Preparing a Tea\" class=\"wp-image-1362\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column --></div></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/spacing {\"clientId\":\"d369595c\",\"height\":{\"desktop\":{\"value\":15,\"unit\":\"px\"}}} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-spacing blockart-spacing-d369595c\"><div class=\"blockart-spacing-inner\"></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/spacing -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The steps of the tea ceremony involve a precise and deliberate process, from the cleansing of utensils to the whisking of the powdered tea. The host, known as the \"chaji,\" follows a prescribed series of movements and gestures, with each action symbolizing a deeper meaning. Guests, in turn, participate in a mindful and respectful manner, appreciating the artistry of the ceremony and the shared moment.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Tea Ceremony', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'tea-ceremony', '', '', '2024-05-07 13:49:48', '2024-05-07 18:49:48', '', 0, 'https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/?post_type=blog&#038;p=1402', 0, 'blog', '', 0),
(1403, 1, '2024-05-06 13:30:30', '2024-05-06 18:30:30', '<!-- wp:kadence/rowlayout {\"uniqueID\":\"1403_c66771-89\",\"columns\":1,\"collapseGutter\":\"skinny\",\"customRowGutter\":[10,\"\",\"\"],\"colLayout\":\"equal\",\"bgImg\":\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/california-maki-on-black-plate-359993-1024x768.jpg\",\"bgImgPosition\":\"43% 50%\",\"padding\":[\"5xl\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],\"kbVersion\":2} -->\n<!-- wp:kadence/column {\"borderWidth\":[\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],\"uniqueID\":\"1403_3b43d5-33\",\"kbVersion\":2} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-column kadence-column1403_3b43d5-33\"><div class=\"kt-inside-inner-col\"><!-- wp:ultimate-post/heading {\"blockId\":\"0605d7\",\"headingText\":\"Sushi\",\"headingStyle\":\"style7\",\"headingTag\":\"h1\",\"headingTypo\":{\"openTypography\":1,\"size\":{\"lg\":\"55\",\"unit\":\"px\"},\"height\":{\"lg\":\"\",\"unit\":\"px\"},\"decoration\":\"none\",\"transform\":\"\",\"family\":\"Poppins\",\"weight\":\"700i\",\"type\":\"sans-serif\"},\"headingColor\":\"#ffffff\",\"headingBorderBottomColor\":\"#ffffff\"} /--></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:kadence/column -->\n<!-- /wp:kadence/rowlayout -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {\"ref\":1421} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/section {\"clientId\":\"9ca5c92f\",\"columns\":2} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-section blockart-section-9ca5c92f\"><div class=\"blockart-container\"><div class=\"blockart-section-inner\"><!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"f125ae94\"} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-f125ae94\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Sushi, an iconic Japanese dish, transcends the realm of food to become a cultural art form celebrated worldwide. At its essence, sushi is a meticulous composition of vinegared rice, fresh seafood, and occasionally vegetables, all carefully arranged to create a symphony of flavors and textures. Nigiri, with its perfectly seasoned rice beneath thin slices of expertly sourced fish, exemplifies the simplicity and precision that characterize traditional sushi. Meanwhile, rolls like maki or temaki showcase the creativity of sushi chefs, incorporating diverse ingredients and imaginative combinations, often wrapped in sheets of nori seaweed. The significance of sushi extends beyond its exquisite taste; it embodies a centuries-old culinary tradition that values seasonality, craftsmanship, and an aesthetic presentation that elevates each dining experience into a sensory journey.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"48864863\"} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-48864863\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":1354,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/close-up-photo-of-sashimi-3298596-684x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Close-Up Photo of Sashimi\" class=\"wp-image-1354\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column --></div></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/spacing {\"clientId\":\"f0401dc8\",\"height\":{\"desktop\":{\"value\":15,\"unit\":\"px\"}}} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-spacing blockart-spacing-f0401dc8\"><div class=\"blockart-spacing-inner\"></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/spacing -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Beyond the palate, sushi dining embraces a communal and social aspect, exemplified by the sushi bar experience where skilled itamae (sushi chefs) engage with patrons directly. The ritual of dipping a piece of sushi into soy sauce, adding a touch of wasabi or pickled ginger, becomes a shared cultural experience. Sushi\'s global popularity not only speaks to its delectable allure but also to its ability to bridge cultures, offering a taste of Japan\'s rich culinary heritage to enthusiasts around the world.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Sushi', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'sushi', '', '', '2024-05-07 13:50:51', '2024-05-07 18:50:51', '', 0, 'https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/?post_type=blog&#038;p=1403', 0, 'blog', '', 0),
(1404, 1, '2024-05-06 13:30:06', '2024-05-06 18:30:06', '<!-- wp:kadence/rowlayout {\"uniqueID\":\"1404_f0cce1-61\",\"columns\":1,\"collapseGutter\":\"skinny\",\"customRowGutter\":[10,\"\",\"\"],\"colLayout\":\"equal\",\"bgImg\":\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/pink-petaled-flowers-closeup-photo-992734-1024x683.jpg\",\"padding\":[\"5xl\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],\"kbVersion\":2} -->\n<!-- wp:kadence/column {\"borderWidth\":[\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],\"uniqueID\":\"1404_a98467-51\",\"kbVersion\":2} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-column kadence-column1404_a98467-51\"><div class=\"kt-inside-inner-col\"><!-- wp:ultimate-post/heading {\"blockId\":\"e5e4e3\",\"headingText\":\"Cherry Blossoms\",\"headingStyle\":\"style7\",\"headingTag\":\"h1\",\"headingTypo\":{\"openTypography\":1,\"size\":{\"lg\":\"55\",\"unit\":\"px\"},\"height\":{\"lg\":\"\",\"unit\":\"px\"},\"decoration\":\"none\",\"transform\":\"\",\"family\":\"Poppins\",\"weight\":\"700i\",\"type\":\"sans-serif\"},\"headingColor\":\"#ffffff\",\"headingBorderBottomColor\":\"#ffffff\"} /--></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:kadence/column -->\n<!-- /wp:kadence/rowlayout -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {\"ref\":1421} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Cherry blossoms hold a unique and revered place in various cultures, with particular significance in Japan. The blooming of cherry blossoms, known as \"sakura\" in Japanese, is an annual spectacle that marks the arrival of spring. What makes cherry blossoms so special is not only their ephemeral beauty but also the cultural and symbolic meanings associated with them.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/section {\"clientId\":\"70fe49ac\",\"columns\":2} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-section blockart-section-70fe49ac\"><div class=\"blockart-container\"><div class=\"blockart-section-inner\"><!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"f86a8d9c\"} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-f86a8d9c\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"right\":\"0\",\"left\":\"0\"},\"padding\":{\"left\":\"0\"}}}} -->\n<p style=\"margin-right:0;margin-left:0;padding-left:0\">Firstly, cherry blossoms symbolize the transient and fragile nature of life. The blossoms bloom for a brief period, usually a week or two, before delicately falling to the ground. This fleeting existence resonates deeply in Japanese philosophy, reminding people to appreciate the beauty of the present moment and to acknowledge the impermanence of all things.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"e3f3292c\"} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-e3f3292c\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:blockart/image {\"clientId\":\"0ccc9168\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/white-cherry-blossom-tree-1008211-1024x683.jpg\",\"id\":1345,\"height\":683,\"width\":1024,\"alt\":\"White Cherry Blossom Tree\"}} -->\n<figure class=\"blockart-image blockart-image-0ccc9168\"><img class=\"wp-image-1345 hover-effect-static filter-none mask mask-none\" src=\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/white-cherry-blossom-tree-1008211-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"White Cherry Blossom Tree\" height=\"683\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/image --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column --></div></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/spacing {\"clientId\":\"8fd55d7a\",\"height\":{\"desktop\":{\"value\":15,\"unit\":\"px\"}}} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-spacing blockart-spacing-8fd55d7a\"><div class=\"blockart-spacing-inner\"></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/spacing -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The cultural significance of cherry blossoms is also tied to their association with renewal and new beginnings. The blossoming of trees coincides with the start of the school year and the fiscal year in Japan, signifying a fresh start and the promise of a hopeful future. This symbolism extends to various aspects of life, encouraging people to embrace change and view it as an opportunity for growth.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Furthermore, the tradition of hanami, which translates to \"flower viewing,\" is an integral part of Japanese culture during the cherry blossom season. Families and friends gather in parks to picnic beneath the blooming trees, appreciating the beauty of the blossoms and celebrating the arrival of spring. The shared experience of hanami fosters a sense of community and connection, making cherry blossoms a symbol not only of nature\'s beauty but also of togetherness and shared joy.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/section {\"clientId\":\"cda69d13\",\"columns\":2} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-section blockart-section-cda69d13\"><div class=\"blockart-container\"><div class=\"blockart-section-inner\"><!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"87739f90\",\"background\":{\"background\":1,\"type\":\"color\",\"image\":{\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/pexels-bagus41-1440476-1-scaled.jpg\",\"id\":1263,\"height\":1707,\"width\":2560},\"position\":{\"desktop\":\"48.00% 0.00%\"}}}} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-87739f90\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:blockart/spacing {\"clientId\":\"5349870f\"} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-spacing blockart-spacing-5349870f\"><div class=\"blockart-spacing-inner\"></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/spacing -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":1263,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/pexels-bagus41-1440476-1-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"Cherry blossoms and temple\" class=\"wp-image-1263\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/column {\"clientId\":\"a2a17c4b\"} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-column blockart-column-a2a17c4b\"><div class=\"blockart-column-inner\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Furthermore, the tradition of hanami, which translates to \"flower viewing,\" is an integral part of Japanese culture during the cherry blossom season. Families and friends gather in parks to picnic beneath the blooming trees, appreciating the beauty of the blossoms and celebrating the arrival of spring. The shared experience of hanami fosters a sense of community and connection, making cherry blossoms a symbol not only of nature\'s beauty but also of togetherness and shared joy.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/column --></div></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:blockart/spacing {\"clientId\":\"10c6f8ac\",\"height\":{\"desktop\":{\"value\":15,\"unit\":\"px\"}}} -->\n<div class=\"blockart-spacing blockart-spacing-10c6f8ac\"><div class=\"blockart-spacing-inner\"></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:blockart/spacing -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In essence, the specialness of cherry blossoms lies in their evocative beauty, their representation of life\'s transience, and the cultural traditions and meanings woven into their delicate petals. They serve as a powerful reminder to cherish the present, embrace change, and find joy in shared experiences.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Cherry Blossoms', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'cherry-blossoms', '', '', '2024-05-07 13:52:53', '2024-05-07 18:52:53', '', 0, 'https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/tozai-hotel/?post_type=blog&#038;p=1404', 0, 'blog', '', 0),
