(192, 1, '2024-05-14 17:18:13', '2024-05-14 17:18:13', '<style>/*! elementor - v3.21.0 - 08-05-2024 */\n.elementor-heading-title{padding:0;margin:0;line-height:1}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title[class*=elementor-size-]>a{color:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-small{font-size:15px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-medium{font-size:19px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-large{font-size:29px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-xl{font-size:39px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-xxl{font-size:59px}</style><h1>WordPress</h1>		\n			<h2>The open source publishing platform of choice for millions of websites worldwide—from creators and small businesses to enterprises.</h2>		\n			<a href=\"https://kbotabara.bitlampsites.com/iwp/final/workshops/\">\n									How to Get Started\n					</a>\n			<h2>WordPress.Com vs WordPress.Org?</h2>		\n		<p>The main difference between the two is that WordPress.org does not include hosting and it is mostly used as a reference that houses information, downloads, resources, and communities to get involved. WordPress.com includes hosting and domains.</p><p><b>What does WordPress.com offer that WordPress.org does not?</b></p><p>WordPress.com takes care of most aspects when creating a website. Compared to WordPress.org, it offers hosting by WordPress and regular backups. It also requires no coding knowledge, so the learning curve for beginners will easier. It is also extremely safe security wise because it is constantly monitored and updated. </p><p><b>What does WordPress.org offer that WordPress.com does not?</b></p><p>WordPress.org is self-hosting so this could offer more freedom when creating a website. Compared to WordPress.com that offers limited SEO, there is no limitations and so this could help create better SEO. There is a